.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt ARCSTATS-EXPORTER 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm arcstats-exporter
.Nd write the ZFS ARC counters where node_exporter will serve them
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads
.Pa /proc/spl/kstat/zfs/arcstats
and writes every row whose value is a whole number as one gauge,
.Ql zfs_arcstat{metric="name"} value ,
to a file in node_exporter's textfile directory.
It writes a temporary file beside the real one and renames it over, so a
scrape never reads half a file.
.Pp
It exists because node_exporter's own ZFS collector fails on current
kernels with
.Dq could not parse expected integer value
for a field it does not know; kldload turns that collector off
.Pq Fl -no-collector.zfs
and reads the kstat directly.
.Pp
.Pa arcstats-exporter.timer
runs it 10 seconds after boot and every 15 seconds after that.
It must run as root to write the file.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print the header comment and exit 0, writing nothing.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /var/lib/node_exporter/textfile_collector/arcstats.prom
What it writes.
.It Pa /etc/systemd/system/node_exporter.service.d/textfile.conf
Points node_exporter at the directory, and turns its ZFS collector off.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when the file is written.
When the kstat cannot be read \(em the ZFS module is not loaded \(em it
exits 2 with the failing line on standard error and leaves the last file
it wrote in place;
.Ql node_textfile_mtime_seconds
shows how old that file is.
.Sh EXAMPLES
On a kldload desktop on 2026-09-30.
The ARC's size against its ceiling, and its hits and misses since boot:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ grep -E 'metric="(size|c_max|hits|misses)"' /var/lib/node_exporter/textfile_collector/arcstats.prom
zfs_arcstat{metric="hits"} 49593778714
zfs_arcstat{metric="misses"} 93809708
zfs_arcstat{metric="c_max"} 8589934592
zfs_arcstat{metric="size"} 8579714552
# (exited 0)
$ grep -c '^zfs_arcstat' /var/lib/node_exporter/textfile_collector/arcstats.prom
148
# (exited 0)
.Ed
.Pp
When the three exporters last ran and will next run:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ systemctl list-timers arcstats-exporter.timer zpool-scrub-exporter.timer kfire-exporter.timer
NEXT                        LEFT LAST                         PASSED UNIT                       ACTIVATES
Wed 2026-09-30 02:41:43 PDT   6s Wed 2026-09-30 02:41:28 PDT  8s ago arcstats-exporter.timer    arcstats-exporter.service
Wed 2026-09-30 02:41:43 PDT   6s Wed 2026-09-30 02:41:28 PDT  8s ago kfire-exporter.timer       kfire-exporter.service
Wed 2026-09-30 02:42:06 PDT  29s Wed 2026-09-30 02:41:06 PDT 30s ago zpool-scrub-exporter.timer zpool-scrub-exporter.service

3 timers listed.
Pass --all to see loaded but inactive timers, too.
# (exited 0)
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr systemd.timer 5 ,
.Xr kfire-exporter 8 ,
.Xr zpool-scrub-exporter 8
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
Every value is a gauge, the counters among them; a dashboard takes
.Fn rate
of
.Ql hits
and
.Ql misses
all the same.
.Pp
The names are the kstat's, not node_exporter's: a query written for
.Ql node_zfs_arc_size
finds nothing here and wants
.Ql zfs_arcstat{metric="size"} .
